:"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T17:33:10Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:33:10Z","body":"Based on what, a 3D node depends on its parent 3D node? Please explain how it should work and how it doesn't","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885896151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885957649","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3885957649","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3885957649,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nnwIR","user":{"login":"DexterFstone","id":92402263,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYHyVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92402263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone","html_url":"https://github.com/DexterFstone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T17:44:54Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:44:54Z","body":"> Based on what, a 3D node depends on its parent 3D node? Please explain how it should work and how it doesn't\n\nIn a 3D scene, any nodes that don't inherit Node3D shouldn't interpolate default transforming behavior. Same for 2D scenes","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885957649/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885976333","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3885976333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3885976333,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nn0sN","user":{"login":"DexterFstone","id":92402263,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYHyVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92402263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone","html_url":"https://github.com/DexterFstone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DexterFstone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T17:49:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:49:00Z","body":"```\nScene (Node3D)\n- Node (Node)\n- - MeshInstance3D (MeshInstance3D)\n```\nThe `MeshInstance3D` should move, rotate, or scale relative to the `Scene`, because the `Node` does not have any transform property, so it's blocking `MeshInstance3D` from transforming relative to `Scene`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885976333/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885980317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3885980317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3885980317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nn1qd","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T17:53:11Z","body":"Yes that's as expected, 3D nodes inherit transform from their 3D *parent* nothing else, having a `Node` as parent is the same as checking `top_level`\n\nThis is [documented for `CanvasItem`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_canvasitem.html#class-canvasitem) but not for 3D nodes so that should be documented more correctly (it's implied but not explictly stated \"Affine operations (translation, rotation, scale) are calculated in the coordinate system relative to the parent\")\n\nBut the scene root has no special meaning here, and I don't think any documentation says it does","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3885980317/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3887323265","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3887323265","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3887323265,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ns9iB","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T21:29:02Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T21:29:02Z","body":"> Yes that's as expected, 3D nodes inherit transform from their 3D _parent_ nothing else, having a `Node` as parent is the same as checking `top_level`\n\nThe thing is, as seen [in the presented video](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issue-3927651384), the preview behavior seems to be broken: note that the instantiated scene's inner MeshInstance3D parented to the plain Node moves when dragging the preview. After the instantiation dragging the same scene instance (so not a preview)  no longer moves the same inner MeshInstance3D (which is the expected behavior as you've explained).\n\nQuick testing, for `top_level=true` the preview behaves correctly (the mesh stays in place; the same as after instantiating):\n\n<img width=\"739\" height=\"399\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b3d0cd6-168a-47b2-9507-403ef127f0ae\" />\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bd8f0714-030c-4e0d-9911-6bc2003d7d4c\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3887323265/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3887538915","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3887538915","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3887538915,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ntyLj","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T22:18:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T08:44:31Z","body":"The question is whether the behavior of assigning the starting position of the sub-node is correct or not (edit: i.e. Retaining the preview). Both behaviors might arguably he expected, but it should indeed behave the same way with `top_level==true` so it should probably be unified one way or the other \n\nGood catch didn't realize that as ironically not part of the reported behavior\n\nWhat's the 2D behavior in the same case?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3887538915/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3887674061","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3887674061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3887674061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7nuTLN","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-11T22:51:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-11T22:51:18Z","body":"> The question is whether the behavior of assigning the starting position of the sub-node is correct or not. Both behaviors might arguably he expected, but it should indeed behave the same way with `top_level==true` so it should probably be unified one way or the other\n\nFor sure the preview should show what will be the state after the instantiation. Currently it lies to the user.\n\nSeems like (some?) non-Node3Ds are being replaced by plain Node3D in the preview:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/40448082abe972daa179c64d7889cd88a8e7ea9c/editor/scene/3d/node_3d_editor_plugin.cpp#L5142-L5150\n\nThis would explain why in the presented example the mesh in the prevew moves with the scene root.\n\nSuch replacement doesn't make much sense to me, it was done in #56362. Seems more like a hack than a proper solution for the original issue (#56361). 🤔 Not sure what was the exact issue / what a proper solution would be.\n\n> What's the 2D behavior in the same case?\n\nWorks as expected (WYSIWYG).\n\n<img width=\"745\" height=\"400\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec5488d8-ec1d-4cdb-9fdf-667dbb67ee1c\" />\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/20896ec8-0609-4e3a-a236-90736b4f1f44","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3887674061/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3889524990","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/116173#issuecomment-3889524990","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116173","id":3889524990,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7n1XD-","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.gith